283
00:16:31,770 --> 00:16:32,640
I'm older than you.

284
00:16:35,580 --> 00:16:37,080
Call me "Third, big guy," would you?

285
00:16:37,330 --> 00:16:38,760
"Third, big guy..."

286
00:16:38,960 --> 00:16:40,280
"Third, big guy..."

287
00:16:46,030 --> 00:16:47,520
So you're just like a big brother to me?

288
00:16:48,140 --> 00:16:49,010
No...

289
00:16:53,360 --> 00:16:54,440
Here, sweetie. Give it a try.

290
00:16:54,460 --> 00:16:55,240
Sure thing.

291
00:16:56,000 --> 00:16:57,860
- Go on. Get the ladle now.
- The ladle, alright.

292
00:16:57,880 --> 00:16:59,020
Grab some noodles.

293
00:16:59,040 --> 00:17:00,300
Do the one with the glove, son.

294
00:17:00,320 --> 00:17:00,940
There...

295
00:17:00,960 --> 00:17:01,960
Not too much, not too much.

296
00:17:02,040 --> 00:17:03,320
- About this much?
- Whoa, that's a lot.

297
00:17:03,340 --> 00:17:04,980
Good. Let's say they ordered
extra noodles.

298
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:05,640
Alright, alright.

299
00:17:05,660 --> 00:17:06,430
There you go.

300
00:17:06,450 --> 00:17:07,920
- Blanch the noodles, go on.
- That's like, extra-extra.

301
00:17:08,089 --> 00:17:09,970
- Scoop it in... Alright, in it goes.
- Right.

302
00:17:09,990 --> 00:17:11,240
- This one first?
- Yes.

303
00:17:11,450 --> 00:17:12,069
I think it's done.

304
00:17:12,089 --> 00:17:12,380
Eek!

305
00:17:12,400 --> 00:17:13,180
- Whoa! What the hell?!
- Whoa!

306
00:17:13,200 --> 00:17:14,160
I think it looks done.

307
00:17:16,040 --> 00:17:17,760
What, Dad? That was so loud.

308
00:17:42,080 --> 00:17:44,340
[Baan Tiew Shop]

309
00:17:48,990 --> 00:17:49,940
Dad, Mom,

310
00:17:49,960 --> 00:17:51,590
anything else I could help you with?

311
00:17:51,610 --> 00:17:52,570
Nothing else, sweetie.

312
00:17:55,260 --> 00:17:56,260
Then...

313
00:17:56,470 --> 00:17:57,880
we're heading back.

314
00:17:58,070 --> 00:17:58,740
What?

315
00:17:59,220 --> 00:18:00,720
Aren't you gonna spend the night?

316
00:18:04,400 --> 00:18:05,200
Well...

317
00:18:05,490 --> 00:18:06,360
what about Third?

318
00:18:06,570 --> 00:18:08,250
What? He can stay in your room?

319
00:18:11,320 --> 00:18:11,920
What's wrong?

320
00:18:14,130 --> 00:18:15,440
Is that a good idea?

321
00:18:17,380 --> 00:18:18,130
Oh!

322
00:18:18,300 --> 00:18:19,120
Right...

323
00:18:19,550 --> 00:18:20,550
Then...

324
00:18:21,470 --> 00:18:23,060
we're heading home now.

325
00:18:23,080 --> 00:18:24,320
I'll visit often.

326
00:18:24,340 --> 00:18:25,360
Okay.

327
00:18:25,380 --> 00:18:26,260
Alright.

328
00:18:29,460 --> 00:18:30,950
- See you.
- Mm.

329
00:18:30,970 --> 00:18:32,000
Oh, jeez...

330
00:18:32,020 --> 00:18:33,360
Can't have you feel left out.

331
00:18:34,350 --> 00:18:35,360
Take care of yourself, son.

332
00:18:35,380 --> 00:18:36,160
Alright.

333
00:18:37,480 --> 00:18:38,480
And who's driving?

334
00:18:38,860 --> 00:18:39,660
I am.

335
00:18:40,560 --> 00:18:41,790
Don't speed.

336
00:18:41,810 --> 00:18:42,460
Of course not.

337
00:18:42,830 --> 00:18:44,110
Alrighty, safe travels, sweeties.

338
00:18:44,130 --> 00:18:45,060
- Alright.
- Alright.

339
00:18:45,080 --> 00:18:45,540
Goodbye.

340
00:18:45,560 --> 00:18:46,600
- Dad, Mom, goodbye.
- Bye, kids.

341
00:18:47,910 --> 00:18:48,680
We'll be waiting.

342
00:18:51,740 --> 00:18:53,740
Why did you bring me here?

343
00:18:55,160 --> 00:18:57,160
I just wanna sit down and talk to you.

344
00:18:58,210 --> 00:18:59,600
Can't we do it in the car?

345
00:19:00,390 --> 00:19:02,170
That wouldn't be romantic, though.

346
00:19:03,480 --> 00:19:04,070
Come on.

347
00:19:05,510 --> 00:19:06,000
Quick!

348
00:19:24,270 --> 00:19:28,360
♫The closer we are, the clearer♫

349
00:19:28,380 --> 00:19:32,210
♫What they call love is such a wonder♫

350
00:19:32,580 --> 00:19:38,470
♫You change my world every time we meet♫

351
00:19:40,370 --> 00:19:44,450
♫I think you've gotten me hooked so well♫

352
00:19:44,470 --> 00:19:48,710
♫My heart is under your spell♫

353
00:19:48,730 --> 00:19:52,680
♫Everything I'm feeling profoundly,♫

354
00:19:52,700 --> 00:19:57,070
♫You make it special
just by being next to me♫

355
00:19:57,090 --> 00:20:01,350
♫I think you've gotten me hooked so well♫

356
00:20:01,370 --> 00:20:05,600
♫Love's right in front of me, I can tell♫

357
00:20:05,630 --> 00:20:09,720
♫You're too heavenly
to be my special someone♫

358
00:20:09,740 --> 00:20:12,420
♫Would you care to spell it out♫

359
00:20:12,440 --> 00:20:16,020
♫If I can call you my love at once?♫

360
00:20:19,390 --> 00:20:20,240
Hey.

361
00:20:21,490 --> 00:20:23,470
When you were a fan,
why did you have to...

362
00:20:23,680 --> 00:20:25,770
wear a cap and a mask?

363
00:20:26,250 --> 00:20:27,280
What?

364
00:20:27,990 --> 00:20:29,770
I was a photographer for hire.

365
00:20:30,260 --> 00:20:32,380
If someone recognized me as a fan,

366
00:20:32,400 --> 00:20:33,760
they wouldn't be okay with it, right?

367
00:20:33,910 --> 00:20:36,080
No one wants fans working there.

368
00:20:37,350 --> 00:20:39,120
But fans need to make a living, too, right?

369
00:20:45,280 --> 00:20:46,780
No one's gonna think the way you do.

370
00:20:53,670 --> 00:20:55,160
Then, let me ask you another question.

371
00:20:55,980 --> 00:20:57,570
What do you think about Nine right now?

372
00:21:02,930 --> 00:21:03,950
Right now?

373
00:21:07,890 --> 00:21:09,170
All I know is...

374
00:21:10,350 --> 00:21:11,800
no matter what happens,

375
00:21:13,040 --> 00:21:14,560
life's gotta go on.

376
00:21:15,790 --> 00:21:17,480
Sometimes, I can't help but wonder

377
00:21:18,480 --> 00:21:20,120
if I would've been happier

378
00:21:20,960 --> 00:21:22,920
had I never met Nine.

379
00:21:29,380 --> 00:21:30,760
Come to think of it...

380
00:21:31,690 --> 00:21:32,680
I don't know...

381
00:21:37,890 --> 00:21:39,720
He was the one who created me.

382
00:21:41,290 --> 00:21:42,210
So, what now?

383
00:21:42,900 --> 00:21:44,280
Are you gonna thank him?

384
00:21:45,820 --> 00:21:47,080
Don't you think the same way I do?

385
00:21:51,400 --> 00:21:53,160
What you're saying is not wrong.

386
00:21:55,100 --> 00:21:56,360
We're on the same page.

387
00:22:05,080 --> 00:22:06,080
Then...

388
00:22:06,420 --> 00:22:07,480
let me ask you a question.

389
00:22:10,170 --> 00:22:12,180
Why did you agree to become
Nine's partner?

390
00:22:14,470 --> 00:22:16,320
Nine, you made the cut for
'The Bet Love's.'

391
00:22:16,720 --> 00:22:17,980
You're not...

392
00:22:18,170 --> 00:22:20,520
getting my hopes up, right, Pitch?

393
00:22:21,120 --> 00:22:21,760
Not at all...

394
00:22:22,250 --> 00:22:23,700
The main leads are TheeJuno,

395
00:22:23,720 --> 00:22:25,000
and you're the secondary couple.

396
00:22:25,900 --> 00:22:27,020
In a bit...

397
00:22:27,620 --> 00:22:28,880
the person who stars opposite you
will be here.

398
00:22:29,750 --> 00:22:30,380
Uh...

399
00:22:30,400 --> 00:22:31,640
Like, right now?

400
00:22:33,180 --> 00:22:34,060
There he is.

401
00:22:34,080 --> 00:22:35,000
Come on in!

402
00:22:43,780 --> 00:22:44,480
Third...

403
00:22:44,500 --> 00:22:46,080
Oh, you two know each other?

404
00:22:51,970 --> 00:22:53,360
I'm not working with him.

405
00:22:56,140 --> 00:22:57,280
That won't be possible, Third.

406
00:22:57,300 --> 00:22:58,840
I'm not playing opposite him,
no matter what.

407
00:22:59,860 --> 00:23:01,520
I'm not asking for your opinion.

408
00:23:02,290 --> 00:23:02,720
Besides,

409
00:23:02,740 --> 00:23:04,520
I've talked to your mom and decided that

410
00:23:04,540 --> 00:23:06,760
you're playing the secondary couple.

411
00:23:12,390 --> 00:23:13,280
Crystal?

412
00:23:16,970 --> 00:23:18,180
We meet again, bud.

413
00:23:19,110 --> 00:23:20,280
Please take care of me.

414
00:23:23,360 --> 00:23:23,900
How come you always do it

415
00:23:23,920 --> 00:23:25,840
without even asking me?

416
00:23:26,350 --> 00:23:27,920
Why do I have to?

417
00:23:28,580 --> 00:23:29,970
What I believe is good for you

418
00:23:30,290 --> 00:23:31,680
will be good for you.

419
00:23:32,350 --> 00:23:33,980
Don't you wanna be an actor?

420
00:23:34,700 --> 00:23:36,840
It's true that I want to, Mom.

421
00:23:37,150 --> 00:23:37,620
But that doesn't mean

422
00:23:37,640 --> 00:23:39,480
I can play opposite just anyone.

423
00:23:41,500 --> 00:23:43,080
That mindset

424
00:23:43,760 --> 00:23:45,120
is why you've never become famous.

425
00:23:47,100 --> 00:23:48,880
If you don't see my worth,

426
00:23:49,990 --> 00:23:51,520
could you at least not look down on me?

427
00:23:52,640 --> 00:23:54,200
Then, I was right

428
00:23:54,690 --> 00:23:56,560
to push for you to play opposite Nine.

429
00:24:01,390 --> 00:24:02,260
It would've been nice

430
00:24:02,280 --> 00:24:04,400
if I were strong enough
to choose my own path.

431
00:24:07,610 --> 00:24:09,000
But you do know that...

432
00:24:09,660 --> 00:24:11,260
the reason she did it

433
00:24:11,280 --> 00:24:12,380
was that she was worried about you?

434
00:25:23,640 --> 00:25:25,100
Thank you so much for today.

435
00:25:25,120 --> 00:25:26,440
I'm so happy.

436
00:25:27,070 --> 00:25:28,370
Thank you, too.

437
00:25:29,460 --> 00:25:30,140
For?

438
00:25:31,880 --> 00:25:33,720
Well, I've never made noodle soup before,

439
00:25:34,180 --> 00:25:35,840
nor have I ever been a vendor.

440
00:25:36,670 --> 00:25:38,760
Your parents were so kind to teach me.

441
00:25:39,380 --> 00:25:40,520
This is so new.

442
00:25:40,700 --> 00:25:41,750
It wasn't hard, was it?

443
00:25:41,770 --> 00:25:43,160
Just blanching the noodles,

444
00:25:43,290 --> 00:25:44,680
not making them from scratch.

445
00:25:47,190 --> 00:25:49,080
But I like that we hung out today.

446
00:25:52,400 --> 00:25:53,520
I do, too.

447
00:25:55,360 --> 00:25:56,560
Then...

448
00:25:59,020 --> 00:26:01,040
Can I come over to your room
for roti sai mai?

449
00:26:04,510 --> 00:26:05,280
No.

450
00:26:18,160 --> 00:26:19,360
Am I doing a good job?

451
00:26:20,900 --> 00:26:22,400
It's covered in grime from your hands.

452
00:26:22,460 --> 00:26:23,320
Have you washed them?

453
00:26:23,760 --> 00:26:25,280
I have!

454
00:26:27,260 --> 00:26:28,880
Or do you want me to feed you
with my mouth?

455
00:26:32,420 --> 00:26:33,640
Cut it...

456
00:26:38,600 --> 00:26:39,400
Say, "Aah..."

457
00:26:40,440 --> 00:26:41,200
Aah...

458
00:26:42,470 --> 00:26:44,640
Aah...

459
00:26:50,030 --> 00:26:53,300
♫Just a gentle, gentle gaze♫

460
00:26:53,320 --> 00:26:54,580
♫On me, on me♫

461
00:26:54,600 --> 00:26:55,710
♫Keep your eyes on me♫

462
00:26:55,730 --> 00:27:00,660
♫Only a gentle gaze, left or right♫

463
00:27:00,680 --> 00:27:04,370
♫If we meet eyes for a while♫

464
00:27:11,490 --> 00:27:14,200
Just as sweet as the last time we kissed...

465
00:27:16,270 --> 00:27:17,540
Enough.

466
00:27:17,560 --> 00:27:19,040
You're moving too fast.

467
00:27:21,450 --> 00:27:22,640
Alright, I'll quit teasing you.

468
00:27:24,640 --> 00:27:25,940
Though, can I ask you one thing?

469
00:27:31,000 --> 00:27:32,960
Can I spend the night with you?

470
00:27:38,060 --> 00:27:38,880
Pretty please?

471
00:27:39,460 --> 00:27:40,300
Please?

472
00:27:44,750 --> 00:27:46,360
Let me think about it.

473
00:28:03,960 --> 00:28:06,520
[Good vibes only]

474
00:28:15,700 --> 00:28:16,540
What's so funny?

475
00:28:16,960 --> 00:28:17,920
I'm looking sharp.

476
00:28:22,980 --> 00:28:24,060
Calling yourself sharp

477
00:28:24,080 --> 00:28:26,200
while bursting the seams of my clothes,
Mr. Third?

478
00:28:26,230 --> 00:28:27,330
Here, let me take some photos.

479
00:28:27,350 --> 00:28:28,440
Hey, wait.

480
00:28:28,700 --> 00:28:30,520
Do you know I charge money...

481
00:28:30,960 --> 00:28:32,260
for taking photos with me?

482
00:28:32,420 --> 00:28:33,400
No more photos, then.

483
00:28:33,430 --> 00:28:34,400
Aw, no...

484
00:28:35,280 --> 00:28:36,060
Let's take photos.

485
00:28:44,270 --> 00:28:47,920
It's weird that
you're acting strange around me.

486
00:28:48,760 --> 00:28:50,920
You're... too lovely for your own good.

487
00:28:54,370 --> 00:28:56,560
Love me tons, then.

488
00:28:58,370 --> 00:28:59,600
Hey, hey, hey,

489
00:28:59,620 --> 00:29:00,480
now you're just being ridiculous.

490
00:29:02,270 --> 00:29:03,440
Did you hit your head?

491
00:29:04,430 --> 00:29:05,490
Why so aggressive when you blush?

492
00:29:07,800 --> 00:29:09,160
If you wanna spend the night,

493
00:29:09,320 --> 00:29:10,560
I have some conditions.

494
00:29:11,780 --> 00:29:13,280
Don't get close to me.

495
00:29:13,780 --> 00:29:15,000
Don't touch me.

496
00:29:19,350 --> 00:29:20,320
You're seriously saying all that

497
00:29:20,340 --> 00:29:21,880
after I already kissed you?

498
00:29:24,020 --> 00:29:24,880
Whatever.

499
00:29:25,870 --> 00:29:26,720
Don't...

500
00:29:27,350 --> 00:29:28,520
touch me!

501
00:29:33,280 --> 00:29:33,960
Wan.

502
00:29:34,200 --> 00:29:34,800
Hm?

503
00:29:35,870 --> 00:29:36,640
What?

504
00:29:40,300 --> 00:29:41,500
Do you trust your man, Wan?

505
00:29:43,350 --> 00:29:45,280
No, no.

506
00:29:45,490 --> 00:29:47,280
Don't call yourself my man.

507
00:29:47,640 --> 00:29:49,360
No, no, no, that's cheesy!

508
00:29:49,900 --> 00:29:50,960
Answer me first.

509
00:29:51,870 --> 00:29:53,080
Do you trust your man, Wan?

510
00:29:56,480 --> 00:29:58,560
Of course, your boy trusts you.

511
00:30:00,760 --> 00:30:01,720
You know?

512
00:30:02,660 --> 00:30:04,440
Back at the audition,

513
00:30:04,590 --> 00:30:06,120
when you helped me out in the restroom,

514
00:30:06,640 --> 00:30:08,400
I still remember how it felt.

515
00:30:09,180 --> 00:30:10,200
If you want it to go away,

516
00:30:10,220 --> 00:30:11,120
listen to me.

517
00:30:12,230 --> 00:30:12,840
One...

518
00:30:13,620 --> 00:30:14,440
Two...

519
00:30:14,880 --> 00:30:15,800
Three...

520
00:30:16,180 --> 00:30:16,720
Four...

521
00:30:19,080 --> 00:30:19,960
How did you feel?

522
00:30:21,040 --> 00:30:22,060
Just like I feel now.

523
00:30:23,960 --> 00:30:25,560
At ease,

524
00:30:26,180 --> 00:30:27,440
trusting you,

525
00:30:27,460 --> 00:30:28,560
warm at heart,

526
00:30:31,550 --> 00:30:33,160
and you really calmed me down.

527
00:30:35,740 --> 00:30:38,000
Even though there's so much
going on right now.

528
00:30:41,900 --> 00:30:43,100
You like being with me, huh?

529
00:30:46,890 --> 00:30:48,160
I think so.

530
00:30:50,120 --> 00:30:51,520
I'm so into you.

531
00:30:54,390 --> 00:30:55,620
I'm so freaking into you.

532
00:31:01,770 --> 00:31:02,760
So you shy away when you blush?

533
00:31:03,060 --> 00:31:03,580
Hm?

534
00:31:05,100 --> 00:31:06,600
Go to bed!

535
00:31:19,430 --> 00:31:21,680
There... I said go to bed.

536
00:31:39,560 --> 00:31:40,600
Go to sleep!

537
00:31:41,610 --> 00:31:42,430
Alright.

538
00:33:44,680 --> 00:33:45,480
Hey!

539
00:33:50,840 --> 00:33:52,280
Don't tell me that...

540
00:33:52,680 --> 00:33:53,800
you guys...

541
00:33:56,220 --> 00:33:56,720
What?

542
00:33:56,740 --> 00:33:57,800
Nothing happened!

543
00:33:58,010 --> 00:34:00,040
Liar. You two were about to kiss.

544
00:34:00,390 --> 00:34:01,120
Or did you...

545
00:34:01,560 --> 00:34:02,320
already kiss?

546
00:34:08,870 --> 00:34:09,719
Kiss?

547
00:34:09,739 --> 00:34:10,840
Quit having your head in the clouds!

548
00:34:11,030 --> 00:34:13,360
Even boulders can't stop shippers.

549
00:34:13,630 --> 00:34:14,989
You can't hide that you're into each other.

550
00:34:15,010 --> 00:34:16,480
Would you stop shipping?!

551
00:34:16,500 --> 00:34:17,480
This is not shipping.

552
00:34:17,500 --> 00:34:20,000
We don't ship real couples!

553
00:34:21,580 --> 00:34:22,530
Get out.

554
00:34:22,550 --> 00:34:23,320
Go!

555
00:34:24,199 --> 00:34:25,340
- Jeez...
- Now.

556
00:34:25,360 --> 00:34:26,360
Fine, I will.

557
00:34:26,380 --> 00:34:28,389
You got it, boss. Let's go full send, chat.

558
00:34:33,920 --> 00:34:35,389
Are they gonna be doomed?

559
00:34:38,449 --> 00:34:39,780
This is giving me a headache.

560
00:34:39,810 --> 00:34:41,040
What, you have a headache?

561
00:34:42,389 --> 00:34:43,199
Ugh...

562
00:34:44,480 --> 00:34:45,679
What do I do?

563
00:35:17,710 --> 00:35:18,680
Hello, you?

564
00:35:19,640 --> 00:35:21,320
I'm already back at my place.

565
00:35:21,610 --> 00:35:23,240
Are you calling just to tell me that?

566
00:35:24,250 --> 00:35:26,320
And have you gone out to eat?

567
00:35:26,730 --> 00:35:27,720
I'm out,

568
00:35:28,100 --> 00:35:29,940
but I'm at the company.

569
00:35:29,960 --> 00:35:31,180
Wut asked for me.

570
00:35:32,110 --> 00:35:33,200
Have you arrived?

571
00:35:33,290 --> 00:35:34,920
I have...

572
00:35:35,380 --> 00:35:35,900
Look...

573
00:35:35,920 --> 00:35:38,040
You kicked me out so soon today.

574
00:35:38,070 --> 00:35:39,600
I could've dropped you off.

575
00:35:42,180 --> 00:35:43,450
Ooh...

576
00:35:45,050 --> 00:35:47,440
Hey, I have to go. Cher's here...

577
00:35:54,660 --> 00:35:55,520
Who was that?

578
00:35:58,370 --> 00:35:59,640
That was my dad.

579
00:35:59,800 --> 00:36:01,320
Should we go inside now?

580
00:36:04,500 --> 00:36:05,280
Your dad?

581
00:36:05,580 --> 00:36:06,100
Why did you grin so widely

582
00:36:06,120 --> 00:36:07,520
while talking to your dad?

583
00:36:08,060 --> 00:36:09,480
Uh...

584
00:36:09,700 --> 00:36:11,140
My dad cracked some jokes.

585
00:36:11,160 --> 00:36:12,190
He said...

586
00:36:12,210 --> 00:36:13,570
he blanched the noodles
Spider-Man style.

587
00:36:13,590 --> 00:36:15,270
Pew, pew, pew, pew!

588
00:36:15,290 --> 00:36:16,280
Pew...

589
00:36:16,440 --> 00:36:17,560
I wanna meet him.

590
00:36:17,970 --> 00:36:19,240
He must be so funny

591
00:36:19,590 --> 00:36:21,040
since you grinned so widely.

592
00:36:22,130 --> 00:36:23,330
- Right.
- Go on in first.

593
00:36:23,350 --> 00:36:24,400
I'll go grab some coffee.

594
00:36:43,520 --> 00:36:46,400
[Can we meet up if you have time?]

595
00:36:49,840 --> 00:36:52,010
[Can we meet up if you have time?

596
00:36:52,030 --> 00:36:54,200
I wanna tell you how sorry
I am for everything]

597
00:37:00,080 --> 00:37:02,040
Renji and Wan...

598
00:37:03,930 --> 00:37:06,380
you're both tapped as Friends of 'MD'

599
00:37:06,400 --> 00:37:08,880
for its upcoming Spin Time model!

600
00:37:10,580 --> 00:37:11,200
Flabbergasted?

601
00:37:11,400 --> 00:37:12,880
Completely shocked and flabbergasted?

602
00:37:12,900 --> 00:37:14,020
Thank Wut!

603
00:37:14,040 --> 00:37:15,020
Go on, thank him.

604
00:37:15,040 --> 00:37:16,200
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

605
00:37:16,540 --> 00:37:17,720
Bless your heart, dear.

606
00:37:18,420 --> 00:37:19,400
Ugh...

607
00:37:19,590 --> 00:37:21,270
After many attempts, at that.

608
00:37:21,290 --> 00:37:22,750
I fought tooth and nail for it!

609
00:37:22,770 --> 00:37:24,560
But we did it!

610
00:37:24,940 --> 00:37:26,760
Is MD the watch brand

611
00:37:26,780 --> 00:37:28,080
that's been going viral lately?

612
00:37:28,260 --> 00:37:29,280
Precisely.

613
00:37:29,360 --> 00:37:29,920
Ooh!

614
00:37:29,940 --> 00:37:31,860
All campaigns launched in Thailand

615
00:37:31,880 --> 00:37:34,200
for one whole year,

616
00:37:34,220 --> 00:37:36,720
you're on board for those!

617
00:37:37,280 --> 00:37:38,320
- Wow...
- Wow...

618
00:37:43,400 --> 00:37:46,240
And you have to work
with ThirdNine for MD.

619
00:37:47,880 --> 00:37:49,400
Brace yourself

620
00:37:49,980 --> 00:37:51,680
and be careful.

621
00:37:53,020 --> 00:37:53,800
It'll be fine.

622
00:37:54,590 --> 00:37:56,760
If you guys have to meet, I'll step up.

623
00:37:57,070 --> 00:37:58,400
Avoid them if you can.

624
00:37:58,920 --> 00:38:00,320
Just see them when you need to, yeah?

625
00:38:01,900 --> 00:38:02,450
Uh, but, like...

626
00:38:02,470 --> 00:38:03,400
So...

627
00:38:04,030 --> 00:38:06,480
What are they gonna do next?

628
00:38:07,280 --> 00:38:07,930
I mean...

629
00:38:09,020 --> 00:38:10,760
are they plotting something?

630
00:38:13,370 --> 00:38:15,040
Come to think of it,

631
00:38:15,780 --> 00:38:19,400
I'm sure they have the receipt.

632
00:38:20,400 --> 00:38:21,540
But I can't wrap my head around

633
00:38:21,560 --> 00:38:22,600
why they're not leaking it.

634
00:38:22,820 --> 00:38:24,080
But I know...

635
00:38:26,510 --> 00:38:28,160
why they're not leaking it.

636
00:38:29,090 --> 00:38:29,840
Hm?

637
00:38:35,820 --> 00:38:36,520
Oh...

638
00:38:37,290 --> 00:38:38,840
I just wanted to say something.

639
00:38:38,860 --> 00:38:39,800
It just looked so cool.

640
00:38:40,110 --> 00:38:40,980
Ugh...

641
00:38:42,350 --> 00:38:43,620
I just wish I could take on the role

642
00:38:43,640 --> 00:38:46,120
of Wan's knight in shining armor.

643
00:38:48,370 --> 00:38:49,040
I'm sorry.

644
00:38:49,170 --> 00:38:49,760
There...

645
00:38:49,900 --> 00:38:50,920
There's your shining armor

646
00:38:50,940 --> 00:38:52,080
awaiting you.

647
00:38:52,160 --> 00:38:53,560
Put it on and set out.

648
00:38:53,810 --> 00:38:55,040
There, take Cher with you.

649
00:38:56,080 --> 00:38:57,330
- Come on.
- What nonsense...

650
00:38:57,350 --> 00:38:58,930
I'll have a word with Wan.

651
00:38:58,950 --> 00:39:00,040
Take your coffee, too.

652
00:39:00,060 --> 00:39:01,460
Oh... I already finished it.

653
00:39:01,480 --> 00:39:02,960
Please throw it away for me. Thanks.

654
00:39:05,240 --> 00:39:06,900
- I'll be waiting downstairs.
- Fabulous!

655
00:39:06,920 --> 00:39:07,920
There...

656
00:39:07,940 --> 00:39:09,000
It's okay, Wut.

657
00:39:09,030 --> 00:39:09,780
I'll... I'll...

658
00:39:09,800 --> 00:39:11,420
Look at that damn boy.

659
00:39:11,440 --> 00:39:13,000
I raised him and shaped him myself.

660
00:39:14,390 --> 00:39:15,680
Don't you follow in his footsteps.

661
00:39:16,160 --> 00:39:16,800
Alright.

662
00:39:18,670 --> 00:39:19,520
Listen, Wan.

663
00:39:21,160 --> 00:39:22,560
I have something important to discuss.

664
00:39:24,820 --> 00:39:25,860
You cannot

665
00:39:26,220 --> 00:39:28,600
make any mistakes on this project.

666
00:39:30,280 --> 00:39:32,560
Whoever has shown themselves
to be your enemy,

667
00:39:32,580 --> 00:39:34,300
keep a close eye on them.

668
00:39:34,320 --> 00:39:35,800
Do not let them out of your sight.

669
00:39:36,180 --> 00:39:37,080
Understood?

670
00:39:40,020 --> 00:39:41,120
Of course, Wut.

671
00:39:45,380 --> 00:39:46,470
This one's okay.

672
00:39:48,170 --> 00:39:48,880
I think that'll work.

673
00:39:49,060 --> 00:39:49,840
Thank you.

674
00:39:50,510 --> 00:39:51,200
Wan.

675
00:39:52,880 --> 00:39:54,200
Renji already headed back.

676
00:39:54,580 --> 00:39:55,820
What did Wut say?

677
00:39:57,600 --> 00:39:59,920
He just repeated that
I couldn't make mistakes.

678
00:40:01,140 --> 00:40:01,860
Mm.

679
00:40:03,110 --> 00:40:04,760
And don't forget to film a perfume review

680
00:40:04,780 --> 00:40:05,640
for the client.

681
00:40:05,940 --> 00:40:06,760
They've chased us up about it.

682
00:40:07,110 --> 00:40:07,660
Sure thing.

683
00:40:07,680 --> 00:40:09,760
I'll get to it as soon as
I get back to my place.

684
00:40:11,000 --> 00:40:12,440
There's one thing to keep in mind

685
00:40:13,130 --> 00:40:14,070
about Nine.

686
00:40:14,770 --> 00:40:16,070
If you see each other again,

687
00:40:16,990 --> 00:40:18,780
keep yourself out of trouble.

688
00:40:19,320 --> 00:40:20,820
Avoid him at all costs if you can.

689
00:40:23,630 --> 00:40:24,900
I'm gonna go talk to Wut.

690
00:40:25,140 --> 00:40:26,360
Tell me whenever you get home.

691
00:40:29,090 --> 00:40:29,680
Alright.

692
00:40:29,860 --> 00:40:30,420
Mm.

693
00:40:37,710 --> 00:40:40,000
Wan, why do you look so stressed out?

694
00:40:41,910 --> 00:40:42,720
Wan?

695
00:40:48,360 --> 00:40:49,880
How did your work meeting go?

696
00:40:53,440 --> 00:40:54,980
Mm... actually,

697
00:40:56,340 --> 00:40:57,890
I got to sign with MD.

698
00:40:58,520 --> 00:40:59,600
Whoa, seriously?

699
00:41:02,010 --> 00:41:04,440
Congrats.

700
00:41:04,700 --> 00:41:05,720
You did such a good job.

701
00:41:06,090 --> 00:41:08,060
That means I'll get to
work with you again,

702
00:41:08,080 --> 00:41:08,860
Mr. Third.

703
00:41:12,230 --> 00:41:13,280
Yes...

704
00:41:13,880 --> 00:41:15,120
Nothing but good things.

705
00:41:15,790 --> 00:41:18,020
So why did you look so stressed out,
Mr. Wan?

706
00:41:18,040 --> 00:41:18,640
Hm?

707
00:41:20,300 --> 00:41:21,240
It was nothing.

708
00:41:22,100 --> 00:41:24,000
Can you drive faster?

709
00:41:24,810 --> 00:41:25,520
It's just...

710
00:41:25,900 --> 00:41:27,600
I have to film a gig for Cher

711
00:41:27,620 --> 00:41:28,760
'cause I forgot.

712
00:41:29,300 --> 00:41:31,000
Jeez, I thought something was
on your mind.

713
00:41:33,000 --> 00:41:34,440
You just forgot to film a gig.

714
00:41:34,520 --> 00:41:35,560
I can definitely help.

715
00:41:36,540 --> 00:41:38,160
I'll film you nicely.

716
00:41:38,470 --> 00:41:39,560
How does that sound?

717
00:41:42,240 --> 00:41:43,040
Good boy.

718
00:42:02,490 --> 00:42:03,970
Tell me about your day.

719
00:42:03,990 --> 00:42:04,690
Hm?

720
00:42:05,390 --> 00:42:06,960
Tell me about your day.

721
00:42:08,360 --> 00:42:09,360
Well...

722
00:42:10,100 --> 00:42:12,420
I signed a contract with MD Watch.

723
00:42:13,690 --> 00:42:14,980
Wan was adorable

724
00:42:15,000 --> 00:42:17,120
when he found out we'd get to sign.

725
00:42:17,310 --> 00:42:19,400
As for Nine, he's been quiet.

726
00:42:20,170 --> 00:42:21,800
Guess he knows about
the video from North.

727
00:42:22,100 --> 00:42:24,600
This is what it's like to
have the upper hand.

728
00:42:26,690 --> 00:42:28,200
Nine's playing second fiddle.

729
00:42:28,890 --> 00:42:29,520
Mm.

730
00:42:30,210 --> 00:42:31,280
The plot has thickened.

731
00:42:32,590 --> 00:42:34,540
Wan seems so much more relieved.

732
00:42:34,980 --> 00:42:37,500
Helping him, I felt like a leading man.

733
00:42:49,210 --> 00:42:50,680
You wanna be Wan's leading man?

734
00:42:56,860 --> 00:42:57,760
I don't.

735
00:42:58,810 --> 00:43:02,620
I wanna be yours alone, babe.

736
00:43:13,210 --> 00:43:13,960
Sulking?

737
00:43:16,020 --> 00:43:17,400
You're acting like a dog.

738
00:43:25,380 --> 00:43:26,600
Wan's dog, huh?

739
00:43:30,330 --> 00:43:31,640
Nope, yours, babe.

740
00:43:31,990 --> 00:43:32,760
Who's your babe?

741
00:43:33,090 --> 00:43:34,080
You're my babe, Time.

742
00:43:34,710 --> 00:43:35,560
I'll let it slide...

743
00:43:46,870 --> 00:43:47,820
So where is View?

744
00:43:48,530 --> 00:43:49,660
Prepping for the exam at her friend's.

745
00:43:49,680 --> 00:43:50,580
She'll be back tomorrow.

746
00:44:03,400 --> 00:44:03,800
Alright.

747
00:44:03,820 --> 00:44:04,600
Okay, let's go.

748
00:44:05,400 --> 00:44:06,100
Okay...

749
00:44:06,600 --> 00:44:07,740
- Ready?
- Mm.

750
00:44:07,760 --> 00:44:08,660
Three...

751
00:44:09,010 --> 00:44:09,880
Two...

752
00:44:10,660 --> 00:44:11,440
Action.

753
00:44:21,510 --> 00:44:22,840
Hanky House's perfume

754
00:44:22,860 --> 00:44:24,630
in Unwritten Letter,

755
00:44:24,650 --> 00:44:27,020
clean-scented, pleasant,
and for everyday use.

756
00:44:27,040 --> 00:44:29,230
You'll smell like you
just showered at all times!

757
00:44:32,240 --> 00:44:33,140
Cut.

758
00:44:34,560 --> 00:44:35,360
That was cute.

759
00:44:37,030 --> 00:44:38,000
Not even a question.

760
00:44:48,540 --> 00:44:48,920
Whoa...

761
00:44:49,400 --> 00:44:50,240
What are you doing?

762
00:45:00,500 --> 00:45:01,320
I think

763
00:45:01,470 --> 00:45:03,040
this fragrance kinda suits you.

764
00:45:10,630 --> 00:45:11,510
What's with you?

765
00:45:12,820 --> 00:45:13,720
Mm!

766
00:45:14,150 --> 00:45:15,200
What's with you?!

767
00:45:17,160 --> 00:45:18,160
Ugh!

768
00:45:22,480 --> 00:45:23,760
Am I making you blush?

769
00:45:26,790 --> 00:45:27,680
Yes.

770
00:45:29,720 --> 00:45:31,000
But... I like it.

771
00:45:32,140 --> 00:45:33,000
You can do it again.

772
00:45:39,830 --> 00:45:40,940
Ugh!

773
00:45:41,280 --> 00:45:42,600
You're being so cheeky.

774
00:45:43,000 --> 00:45:44,270
Just head back to your place now.

775
00:45:45,490 --> 00:45:46,880
How could I?

776
00:45:47,190 --> 00:45:48,960
I haven't even eaten anything.

777
00:45:50,580 --> 00:45:52,360
Are you kicking me out
after I did you a favor?

778
00:45:54,460 --> 00:45:55,230
I'm...

779
00:45:55,600 --> 00:45:56,320
hungry.

780
00:46:06,180 --> 00:46:07,360
Well...

781
00:46:08,650 --> 00:46:09,680
what do you feel like?

782
00:46:19,770 --> 00:46:20,880
Whatever you make,

783
00:46:22,200 --> 00:46:23,520
I'll eat it.

784
00:46:35,050 --> 00:46:35,880
Seriously?

785
00:46:38,220 --> 00:46:39,880
This is all I have here.

786
00:46:40,690 --> 00:46:41,680
Are you eating it or not?

787
00:46:51,000 --> 00:46:52,000
Hey, wait!

788
00:46:53,910 --> 00:46:55,040
I don't do spicy...

789
00:46:55,510 --> 00:46:57,680
I'm only adding a bit in for color.

790
00:46:58,700 --> 00:47:00,120
- Mm, mm.
- That's right...

791
00:47:00,360 --> 00:47:02,320
Just this much.
Pick it out if you're not eating it.

792
00:47:06,400 --> 00:47:07,800
Do you like watching movies?

793
00:47:08,580 --> 00:47:09,920
Movies?

794
00:47:10,100 --> 00:47:11,360
Not really.

795
00:47:11,650 --> 00:47:12,880
I'm fine watching them, though.

796
00:47:13,480 --> 00:47:14,140
If I had to guess,

797
00:47:14,160 --> 00:47:15,880
you like watching movies, right?

798
00:47:17,300 --> 00:47:18,480
Yes, I do.

799
00:47:19,500 --> 00:47:21,040
Barely anyone was home,

800
00:47:22,390 --> 00:47:23,960
so movies kept me company.

801
00:47:24,790 --> 00:47:26,780
Your family must be so busy.

802
00:47:27,580 --> 00:47:29,100
Your mom is a politician,

803
00:47:29,120 --> 00:47:30,120
so what about your dad?

804
00:47:31,290 --> 00:47:32,120
He's a doctor.

805
00:47:32,990 --> 00:47:33,990
Wow...

806
00:47:34,010 --> 00:47:35,520
What a perfect freaking family.

807
00:47:45,890 --> 00:47:46,600
Hey?

808
00:47:49,990 --> 00:47:50,720
Then...

809
00:47:50,960 --> 00:47:52,240
wanna watch a movie tonight?

810
00:47:52,610 --> 00:47:53,640
If you want to, that is.

811
00:47:56,310 --> 00:47:56,920
I do.

812
00:48:03,200 --> 00:48:04,800
So, what movie should we watch?

813
00:48:05,880 --> 00:48:07,480
There's this one movie I really like.

814
00:48:08,500 --> 00:48:10,800
It inspired me to be who I am today.

815
00:48:13,880 --> 00:48:14,720
What is it?

816
00:48:17,200 --> 00:48:18,720
Have you ever seen 'Forrest Gump'?

817
00:48:19,960 --> 00:48:21,640
Once, I think.

818
00:48:23,100 --> 00:48:24,480
But it's been a really long time.

819
00:48:24,710 --> 00:48:25,880
I don't really recall it.

820
00:48:25,990 --> 00:48:27,440
Didn't it come out way
before we were born?

821
00:48:28,800 --> 00:48:29,680
It did.

822
00:48:30,080 --> 00:48:31,800
I saw it for the first time back in 11th grade.

823
00:48:32,800 --> 00:48:34,640
I still remember how it felt.

824
00:48:35,570 --> 00:48:37,280
And I really like Tom Hanks.

825
00:48:38,660 --> 00:48:40,080
He's the best.

826
00:48:40,220 --> 00:48:41,120
No matter what role,

827
00:48:41,140 --> 00:48:42,360
he seems to become one
with the character.

828
00:48:42,810 --> 00:48:44,720
Also, he's true to himself,

829
00:48:45,010 --> 00:48:46,360
never embodying anything
he doesn't believe in.

830
00:48:48,760 --> 00:48:50,320
Or maybe I wanted an escape
from myself?

831
00:48:50,580 --> 00:48:51,720
That's why I chose this career.

832
00:48:52,820 --> 00:48:53,840
Mm...

833
00:48:55,200 --> 00:48:56,640
Are you a Tom Hanks fanboy?

834
00:48:59,110 --> 00:49:00,040
You could say that.

835
00:49:00,780 --> 00:49:02,240
I aspire to be the kind of actor he is.

836
00:49:03,080 --> 00:49:04,720
It's like he lit a firework in my heart.

837
00:49:05,220 --> 00:49:06,980
After watching him for some time, I felt...

838
00:49:07,760 --> 00:49:09,700
I wanted to impress people
with my acting,

839
00:49:09,720 --> 00:49:10,490
just like he does.

840
00:49:15,010 --> 00:49:16,560
So, since you started acting,

841
00:49:16,680 --> 00:49:17,500
has there been any coworker

842
00:49:17,520 --> 00:49:18,600
who's impressed you?

843
00:49:20,230 --> 00:49:21,920
I have to admit...

844
00:49:22,410 --> 00:49:24,200
I don't really follow foreign actors.

845
00:49:29,000 --> 00:49:31,000
Actually, I had a senior
whom I deeply respected.

846
00:49:32,440 --> 00:49:33,320
Who?

847
00:49:35,700 --> 00:49:36,480
Oh?

848
00:49:37,480 --> 00:49:38,420
Something stressing you out, Third?

849
00:49:44,410 --> 00:49:45,120
What's wrong?

850
00:49:45,580 --> 00:49:47,000
Anything you wanna talk about?

851
00:49:47,460 --> 00:49:48,460
You can tell me anything.

852
00:49:48,480 --> 00:49:49,320
I won't charge.

853
00:49:53,960 --> 00:49:55,880
Just the same old fight with my family.

854
00:49:56,590 --> 00:49:57,590
It's about...

855
00:49:58,570 --> 00:50:00,240
your mom not wanting you
to be an actor, right?

856
00:50:02,590 --> 00:50:04,440
I've tried to explain to her,

857
00:50:05,790 --> 00:50:07,370
but she wouldn't listen.

858
00:50:09,100 --> 00:50:10,860
She said this would be the last project.

859
00:50:11,590 --> 00:50:12,840
If I don't take off this time...

860
00:50:13,500 --> 00:50:15,080
she'll have me do something else.

861
00:50:18,290 --> 00:50:19,320
What about 'The Deep Between Us'?

862
00:50:21,190 --> 00:50:22,760
I'm here. I'll help you.

863
00:50:28,050 --> 00:50:29,490
First, stop worrying.

864
00:50:31,100 --> 00:50:32,280
I already read the script.

865
00:50:32,580 --> 00:50:33,440
A buttload of fun.

866
00:50:33,740 --> 00:50:35,080
The secondary couple's well-written.

867
00:50:36,690 --> 00:50:37,560
Honestly,

868
00:50:38,510 --> 00:50:39,800
